menu "ESP32-S3-USB-OTG board"

choice GATEWAY_USB_HOST_POWER_SOURCE
    prompt "USB Type-A host VBUS source"
    default GATEWAY_USB_HOST_POWER_USB_DEV
    help
        The ESP32-S3-USB-OTG Type-A female HOST port is not powered from the
        Micro-USB debug/power connector. Select the actual host VBUS source.

config GATEWAY_USB_HOST_POWER_USB_DEV
    bool "USB_DEV 5 V input (recommended bench setup)"
    help
        Use 5 V supplied through the board's USB_DEV Type-A male connector.

config GATEWAY_USB_HOST_POWER_BATTERY
    bool "On-board battery boost converter"
    help
        Use an attached Li-ion battery and enable the board boost converter.

config GATEWAY_USB_HOST_POWER_OFF
    bool "Leave host VBUS disabled"
    help
        Use only when the downstream topology has been verified to work without
        upstream VBUS. Some self-powered hubs still require host VBUS for attach
        or session detection, so USB_DEV remains the safer default with a hub.

endchoice

endmenu
